  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Sound
  </title>
  <p>
    Orca can use non-speech audio cues and beeps to indicate progress-bar changes. Progress-bar
    beeps rise in pitch as progress increases. Additional sound features are planned for an
    upcoming release.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-sound">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <section id="settings-sound-sound-presenter-sound-output">
      <title>Sound</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Sound</gui> category.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Sound support</gui>: Turns sound output
            on or off. Default: on.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Volume</gui>: Sets the volume for Orca
            sounds. Default: 0.5. Range: 0.0 to 1.0.
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
    <section id="settings-sound-sound-presenter-progress-bars">
      <title>Progress Bars</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Sound</gui> category, <gui>Progress Bars</gui> group.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Beep updates</gui>: Controls whether
            Orca periodically beeps for progress-bar updates. Default: off.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Frequency (secs):</gui> Sets the minimum
            number of seconds between updates for the same progress bar. Zero removes this
            minimum delay. Default: 0. Range: 0 to 100.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Applies to:</gui> Selects which progress
            bars provide updates. Choices: All, Application, Window.
          </p>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>All</gui>: Progress bars in all
                applications.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Application (default)</gui>: Progress bars in
                the active application.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Window</gui>: Progress bars in the
                active window.
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
